<simplesect kind="return"><para>An object that evaluates to true if all the operand expressions are true.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-logical-functions_1gab9b9c26860ceafc1288ecb415f52aaaf" kindref="member">all_of</ref></computeroutput> function template provides a generic logical conjunction for any expression types. It constructs a <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1and__op" kindref="compound">detail::and_op</ref></computeroutput> logical conjunction object, which evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if all the operands are true. For more than two operands, the objects are nested from the left, <computeroutput>(a and b) and c</computeroutput>, and the expression formatter writes them as a single chain, <computeroutput>(a and b and c)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>All the operands are evaluated before the check, so, unlike the standard algorithm of the same name, the function does not stop at the first operand that is false.</para>
<para>The name is the same as that of <computeroutput>std::all_of</computeroutput>: after a <computeroutput>using namespace std</computeroutput>, an unqualified call with three or more operands of the same type selects the standard algorithm, so the function must be called as <computeroutput>mt::all_of()</computeroutput>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
